 "case": {
  "id": "tp53-lfs",
  "title": "A family with early cancers",
  "brief": "<p><b>Referral from the breast clinic.</b> A woman of 33 had HER2-positive breast cancer at 29. Her brother had an osteosarcoma at 15. Her mother had breast cancer at 36 and died at 39; a maternal aunt had a leiomyosarcoma at 41; her maternal grandfather died of a glioblastoma at 46.</p><p>Testing for Li-Fraumeni syndrome (the <i>TP53</i> and <i>POT1</i> panel) found a heterozygous variant in <i>TP53</i>: NM_000546.6:c.818G&gt;A p.(Arg273His). Since then her brother and her maternal aunt have been tested and carry it; her maternal uncle, well at 55, does not. Her sister, well at 30, has not been tested.</p>",
  "tasks": [
   "Open the variant and go through its evidence: frequency, predictions, the protein (is codon 273 a hotspot?), ClinVar and the literature.",
   "On the Family tab, check the relatives’ genotypes, then use the segregation calculator on the variant’s page: is PP1 met, and at what strength?",
   "Classify the variant and sign it; then compare your criteria with the ClinGen TP53 expert panel’s.",
   "Write the report. What would you offer her sister?"
  ],
  "source": "Variant: NM_000546.6(TP53):c.818G>A, GRCh38 17-7673802-C-T, ClinGen allele CA000434. ClinVar VCV000012366; ClinGen TP53 VCEP classification (Evidence Repository). Checked October 2026. The patient and family are fictional."
 },
